Every git commit in this repository belongs to Tony B. Do not use Cursor Agent or any other identity as author or committer.

- Name: `Tony B`
- Email: `krakjn@gmail.com`

Before committing, set the repo identity (once per clone) and pass it on the commit command:

```bash
git config user.name "Tony B"
git config user.email "krakjn@gmail.com"
git -c user.name="Tony B" -c user.email="krakjn@gmail.com" commit --reset-author ...
```

Do not add a `Co-authored-by` trailer. The commit author is already Tony B.
